<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Ammonia beccarii Turing wavelength at 31 µm, Holocene 0 Ma — Code-to-model traceability: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "jacobian, sigma_of_k2, gamma_for_wavelength, linear_mode_check, simulate_field, wavelength_sweep, and ablation_controls each implement one stated equation. The Lean module cites the same integer encodings (744769*5 > 208*15625, 600000/31370 = 19, pore < detail < test, series 1/1 at age 0). No equation number from Turing 1952 is quoted in a comment next to the stencil." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Ammonia beccarii Turing wavelength at 31 µm, Holocene 0 Ma — Model fidelity to source: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The script implements the Schnakenberg steady state, Jacobian, Turing inequality, critical wavenumber k_c² = γ (Dv f_u + Du g_v) / (2 Du Dv), and λ_c = 2π/k_c, with γ solved so λ_c = 31.37 µm. The linearised Fourier monodromy matches analytical σ at Pearson r = 0.9999997 (RMSE about 2.5e-5 /τ after rounding in the sidecar). Equal diffusion gives σ(k_c) = −0.055. Four Lean theorems encode the margin, the 19-wavelength count, the pore/detail/test ordering, and the Holocene terminal; they were not kernel-checked because Lean 4 is not installed. The kinetics are Schnakenberg's, not a foraminiferal calcification law." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Ammonia beccarii Turing wavelength at 31 µm, Holocene 0 Ma — Morphometric validation: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Linear σ matches the monodromy at r = 0.9999997. The γ sweep matches at r = 0.995 (RMSE 0.94 µm). The 160² saturated FFT peak is 32.88 µm against the linear target 31.37 µm (4.8% longer; not a copy of the reference). Spot-spacing CV is 0.14 and the KS distance to Normal(31.37 µm, band half-width) is 0.27. The plate yields 6 tests. Bounding-box diameters average 769.7 µm against the caption ~600 µm (reference 600, value not equal). Foreground fraction 0.420 versus the full-resolution signature 0.440. Coherency at σ = 1.6 px is 0.576 versus 0.487 at σ = 2.8 px. The diameter offset is the open gap." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-diffusion-ablation-std-ratio>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-dispersion-ks-statistic>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-dispersion-rmse>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-equal-diffusion-control-sigma-max>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-gamma-sweep-predicted-vs-measured-wavelength-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-linear-dispersion-pearson-r-vs-numerical-fourier-growth>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-saturated-spot-wavelength>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-segmented-test-count>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-foreground-fraction>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-segmented-mean-test-diameter>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-structure-tensor-coherency>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-spot-spacing-cv>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Ammonia beccarii Turing wavelength at 31 µm, Holocene 0 Ma — MorphoEval overall 85.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Schnakenberg reaction-diffusion on a 600 µm periodic face. γ is solved so the linear critical wavelength is 31.37 µm (3.137e-05 m, log10 −4.503), the 31 µm detail tier. Dv/Du = 10.4 keeps the unstable band at 26.9–39.1 µm. The pore diameter 0.564 µm and the whole-test mode 600 µm fall outside that band. Chronoseries Ammonia 1/1 at 0 Ma has no other age. A six-point γ sweep tracks λ with Pearson r = 0.995. The linearised Fourier monodromy matches σ(k) at r = 1.000. The Hillewaert CC BY-SA plate is segmented (6 tests) and the activator is grown inside those tests across 12 frames at 720×540. Bounding-box diameters average 770 µm against the caption's ~600 µm. Overall 85.5/100 (faithfulness 84.7, reproducibility 87.3); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit a491e0e4871f38b92696ac7909d8a014270fb92c; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 86, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/ammonia_beccarii_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0.py at a491e0e4871f38b92696ac7909d8a014270fb92c, image/png, 813963 B, 1344×1032 px, artifact_sha256 2f66f42e479d98dc781b1aa79e81a123c69b021af59729252835c28b110ba765 (sha256 2f66f42e479d98dc781b1aa79e81a123c69b021af59729252835c28b110ba765), spec_fingerprint 5c78fef63a2342ef4c8a82571c976eb61e437c0ace429ce768a5b9e0809b609e. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 5c78fef63a2342ef4c8a82571c976eb61e437c0ace429ce768a5b9e0809b609e; artifact_sha256: 2f66f42e479d98dc781b1aa79e81a123c69b021af59729252835c28b110ba765; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/ammonia_beccarii_turing_wavelength_s0/Ammonia_beccarii_Hillewaert_2012.jpg=c15a90be96e2b088..., datasets/ammonia_beccarii_turing_wavelength_s0/ammonia_beccarii_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=6a6a4fb506092514..., datasets/ammonia_beccarii_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=5ac93aba84d88754..., datasets/ammonia_beccarii_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=12dc86d6408aac7a...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 dispersion relation and critical wavenumber | Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics | Hillewaert 2012 caption diameter ~600 µm, 500 µm scale bar, CC BY-SA 4.0 plate | Subba & Ghosh 2023 pore diameter 0.564 µm and pore density 0.155 µm⁻² for Ammonia cf. beccarii | Petersen et al. 2016 pore frame of 562 µm² | Hayward et al. 2004 and Schönfeld et al. 2021 limits on the name A. beccarii; reconstructed_in_script: γ chosen so linear λ_c = 31.37 µm | Dv = 10.4 µm²/τ narrow band | Nonlinear field, γ sweep, equal-diffusion control, γ = 0 ablation | Segmentation of the plate and mapping of the field onto each test; transfer_boundary: Pigment-stripe / ocellus cohort language is transferred onto calcite pustule spacing | AFM pore numbers are Ammonia cf. beccarii, not the photographed North Sea individuals | 31.37 µm is the Delphi detail-scale assignment, not a spacing tabulated for this species; does_not_claim: That Ammonia beccarii has pigment ocelli | That 31.37 µm equals the pore diameter | That a predecessor or successor chronospecies exists in this 1/1 series | That the species-gallery Caryophyllia file is Ammonia | That the North Sea photograph is a sequenced Adriatic type." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Bounding-box diameter averages 770 µm against the caption ~600 µm because gray>0.08 includes the bright rim. Remeasure on a rim-excluded mask and report both.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'The 160² saturated FFT wavelength is 32.88 µm, 4.8% above λ_c = 31.37 µm. Show grid convergence against the 96² sweep point (31.18 µm at the same γ).'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Single assessor (grok-4.7). No second provider scored this pass.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R4', 'item': 'Lean 4 is not installed; the four theorems were not kernel-checked.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.55e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Ammonia beccarii Turing wavelength at 31 µm, Holocene 0 Ma — Parameter expressivity: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "γ factors 0.70–1.80 move the predicted wavelength from 37.5 to 23.4 µm and the measured FFT wavelength from 38.7 to 23.0 µm (Pearson r = 0.995, RMSE 0.94 µm), in the direction λ ∝ γ^(−1/2). Setting Dv = Du yields σ(k_c) < 0. Setting γ = 0 drops the noise standard deviation to 0.12 of its initial value. a and b are fixed, not swept." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-ammonia-beccarii-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

